3. JavaScript (script.js):

```javascript
function printDialog() {
    // Hide all other page content
    document.body.style.visibility = 'hidden';

    // Show the dialog
    document.getElementById('dialog').classList.remove('hidden');

    // Open print dialog
    window.print();

    // Restore visibility and hide the dialog after printing
    document.body.style.visibility = 'visible';
    document.getElementById('dialog').classList.add('hidden');
}
```

When the "Print" button is clicked, it will hide all other content on the page by setting the `visibility` property of the body to "hidden". Then, it will remove the "hidden" class from the dialog, making it visible. The `print()` function is called to open the print dialog. After printing, the visibility is restored, and the dialog is hidden again by adding the "hidden" class.

To stretch the form to the end of the page, you can update the CSS for the form element within the dialog. Add the following CSS styles to the existing `styles.css` file:

```css
#dialog form {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    flex-direction: column;
}
```

This CSS will make the form element span the entire width and height of the dialog container. Additionally, it centers the form vertically and horizontally using flexbox properties.

With this change, the form inside the dialog will take up the full width and height of the page when the "Print" button is clicked.

